# Xianshuihe compset: third-party strain-rate data and mesh-specific derived
# products. GSRM v2.1 is CC-BY-NC-SA GEM data with a stable download
# (fetch_strain_rate.sh); xianshuihe_strain_loading.csv is regenerated per
# mesh by strain_rate_loading.py --case and is stale the moment the mesh
# changes, so neither belongs in the repo.
compset/xianshuihe.gmsh.lite/strain_rate_input/GSRM_v2.1_*.txt
compset/xianshuihe.gmsh.lite/xianshuihe_strain_loading.csv

# Xianshuihe compset: only three figures are kept in the repo -- the fault
# trace, the GSRM strain map, and the on-fault loading (Fig 2). Everything else
# the scripts emit (vector duplicates, step-over maps, mesh views) is
# regenerable and stays out.
compset/xianshuihe.gmsh.lite/*.pdf
compset/xianshuihe.gmsh.lite/xianshuihe_step_overs.*
compset/xianshuihe.gmsh.lite/xianshuihe_mesh*.png
